GOVERNMENT OF INDIA 
MINISTRY OF EDUCATION 
DEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION 

LOK SABHA 

UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 174 
ANSWERED ON 21.07.2025 

Caste-based Discrimination/Violence in Campuses 

174    Smt. Kanimozhi Karunanidhi: 

Will the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: 

(a) whether Equal Opportunity Cells have been constituted in Central Universities as per UGC 
(Promotion of Equity in Higher Educational Institutions) Regulations, 2012; 

(b) if so, the details thereof and the number of Central Universities that have created such Cells; 
(c) if not, the reasons for non-constitution of such Cells; 
(d) whether the Government maintains data on instances of caste -based discrimination in 
College/University campuses; 
(e) if so, the details of such incidents in Central Universities during last five years and the current 
year, College-wise/University-wise; 
(f) if not, the reasons therefor; 
(g) the details of support provided by the University or Government to those students who faced 
discrimination; 
(h) whether the Government plans to place any additional mechanisms to address grievances arising 
out of caste-based discrimination; and 
(i) if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?
